    "tags": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>(18th Level) Once per Soma Break, when you remove or negate something, you may declare:</p><p><strong>Total Redaction.</strong></p><p>Within scope:</p><ul><li><p>Summons cannot be re-summoned by that source for a time.</p></li><li><p>Curses cannot reattach.</p></li><li><p>Teleport anchors fail.</p></li><li><p>Reanimation attempts collapse.</p></li></ul><p>This does <strong>not</strong>:</p><ul><li><p>Erase canon.</p></li><li><p>Kill immortals.</p></li><li><p>Undo narrative Lore.</p></li></ul><p>It enforces finality within your jurisdiction.</p><p>Major misfire risk.<br />Backlash guaranteed.</p><p>Redactors don’t erase existence.</p><p>They erase permissions.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
